Verdict: FAIL

The core parse fix is sound — line_is_gradable correctly refuses outcome-less lines, and I confirmed all 141 lines of the live .yoyo/risk_validations.jsonl carry hits arrays, so no real event is dropped by the change.

But the reporting half never fires in the case that matters. src/commands_risk.rs:1182 still has the pre-existing arm:

```rust
ValidationLedger::Present { dropped: 0, .. } => None,
```

which is matched before both new ungradable arms. So a ledger with 0 unparseable lines and N ungradable ones prints nothing — the lines are excluded from the denominator silently, which is precisely the defect the work was meant to eliminate ("count it out loud instead of manufacturing a 0/0", per its own comment). Corrupt JSON is the rare shape; valid-JSON-without-outcome is the shape #764 names, and that's the one now silenced.

The new tests only exercise the parse side; none drives ledger_health_line with dropped == 0, ungradable > 0, which is why this passed green.

Also: CLAUDE.md still asserts the old behavior verbatim ("still absorbed by unwrap_or ... counts as a healthy event", "#764 stays open on both") and wasn't updated in this commit.

Fix is one line — move or narrow the dropped: 0 arm to Present { dropped: 0, ungradable: 0, .. } — plus a test at the emission point.
